    "q-39201": {
      "dom_id": "step-q39201",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "If $u=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\,,$ $v=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\,,$ and $u\\cdot v=22,$ then $\\frac{(3u)\\cdot v}{u\\cdot (2u)}=$",
      "worked_solution": "We will use the fact that the dot product is linear.\n\nTo quickly compute the numerator $3u\\cdot v,$ we multiply $u\\cdot v$ by $3.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3u)\\cdot v & =3(u\\cdot v) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 22 \\\\  & =66.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo quickly compute the denominator $u\\cdot (2u),$ we compute $u\\cdot u$ first and then multiply the result by $2.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot (2u) & =2(u\\cdot u) \\\\  & =2({u}_{1}^{2}+{u}_{2}^{2}+{u}_{3}^{2}+{u}_{4}^{2}) \\\\  & =2({2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{5}^{2}) \\\\  & =2(4+1+9+25) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 39 \\\\  & =78.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{(3u)\\cdot v}{u\\cdot (2u)}=\\frac{66}{78}=\\frac{11}{13}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-39201-a",
