    "q-39196": {
      "dom_id": "step-q39196",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Find $(2a+5b)\\cdot c+(b+3c)\\cdot d,$ if $c\\cdot a=2,$ $b\\cdot c=3,$ $b\\cdot d=4$ and $d\\cdot c=1.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the fact that the dot product is linear in the first variable, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2a+5b)\\cdot c+(b+3c)\\cdot d & =(2a)\\cdot c+(5b)\\cdot c+b\\cdot d+(3c)\\cdot d \\\\  & =2(a\\cdot c)+5(b\\cdot c)+b\\cdot d+3(c\\cdot d).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we can use the fact that the dot product is symmetric to get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(a\\cdot c)+5(b\\cdot c)+b\\cdot d+3(c\\cdot d) & =2(c\\cdot a)+5(b\\cdot c)+b\\cdot d+3(d\\cdot c).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the values for $c\\cdot a,$ $b\\cdot c,$ $b\\cdot d,$ and $d\\cdot c,$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(c\\cdot a)+5(b\\cdot c)+b\\cdot d+3(d\\cdot c) & =2(2)+5(3)+4+3(1) \\\\  & =4+15+4+3 \\\\  & =26.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $(2a+5b)\\cdot c+(b+3c)\\cdot d=26.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
