    "q-139951": {
      "dom_id": "step-q139951",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "If $\\alpha \\beta =-8$ and $b\\cdot a=\\frac{15}{2}$, then what is $(\\alpha a)\\cdot (\\beta b)+12?$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the fact that the dot product is linear in both variables, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\alpha a)\\cdot (\\beta b)+12 & =\\alpha (a\\cdot \\beta b)+12 \\\\  & =\\alpha \\beta (a\\cdot b)+12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, using that the dot product is symmetric, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\alpha \\beta (a\\cdot b)+12 & =\\alpha \\beta (b\\cdot a)+12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute the values for $\\alpha \\beta $ and $b\\cdot a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\alpha \\beta (b\\cdot a)+12 & =(-8)\\cdot \\frac{15}{2}+12 \\\\  & =-60+12 \\\\  & =-48\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
