    "q-74050": {
      "dom_id": "step-q74050",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "Suppose $(a+b)\\cdot a=0$, where $a\\ne 0.$ Which of the following statements are true? \n\nI. $b\\cdot a<0$\n\nII. $b\\cdot a=3$\n\nIII. $a\\cdot a=-3$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true while statement II is false. Simplifying the expression $(a+b)\\cdot a=0$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(a+b)\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ a\\cdot a+b\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ b\\cdot a & =-a\\cdot a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nSince $a\\ne 0$ implies that $a\\cdot a>0$, we obtain that $-a\\cdot a<0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $a\\ne 0,$ we must have $a\\cdot a>0.$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
