    "q-39204": {
      "dom_id": "step-q39204",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "Suppose $(9a+3b)\\cdot a=0$, where $a\\ne 0.$ Which of the following statements are true? \n\nI. $b\\cdot a=3(a\\cdot a)$\n\nII. $a\\cdot a<0$\n\nIII. $b\\cdot a=1$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Simplifying the expression $(9a+3b)\\cdot a=0$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(9a+3b)\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ (9a)\\cdot a+(3b)\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ 9(a\\cdot a)+3(b\\cdot a) & =0 \\\\ 3(b\\cdot a) & =-9(a\\cdot a) \\\\ b\\cdot a & =-3(a\\cdot a)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $a\\ne 0,$ we must have $a\\cdot a>0.$\n\n- Statement III is false since it leads to a contradiction. If $b\\cdot a=1$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(9a+3b)\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ 9(a\\cdot a)+3(b\\cdot a) & =0 \\\\ 9(a\\cdot a)+3(1) & =0 \\\\ a\\cdot a & =-\\frac{1}{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nbut this is a contradiction since $a\\ne 0$ implies that $a\\cdot a>0.$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that none of the statements are true.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
